{
  "notes": [
    "Every frame that is not a rig part (SPEC §12.10). Key = frame name (path under its category folder, no .svg).",
    "anchor: the placement and y-sort point in the file's own units. Stalls anchor at the counter's front edge (SPEC §12.2); characters stand at the rig foot (20, 55).",
    "layer: ground, world (y-sorted) or overlay (SPEC §12.2). ppu: atlas px per unit at 1× (stalls, gate and stocks draw at 3 px per unit like the 640 × 360 layout reference ×3; characters and effects at about 1.8).",
    "Tint variables (--canopy on the stall frame, --player on the reveal ring) become their own white layers, tinted at draw time.",
    "Files with \"reference\" in the name are composed references, not frames.",
    "TF1-fix-1: confetti/piece-<n> are the six pieces of confetti-pieces.svg, one per file (copied verbatim, same viewBox), anchored at each piece's center so they spin and fall alone. stocks-occupied-reference is the one composed reference used as a frame: a thief in the stocks (front view), its --tunic, --skin and --hair tinted from the occupant's outfit."
